WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.208
&lt;i&gt;Ozark &lt;/i&gt;season four part one
is finally on Netflix,

00:00:03.292 --> 00:00:04.708
bringing the moody intrigue,

00:00:04.792 --> 00:00:07.458
rural retaliations
and unexpected twists

00:00:07.542 --> 00:00:09.667
we've come to know and love
from the show.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.292
When my uncle first told me
about

00:00:11.375 --> 00:00:12.583
your disagreement
with Helen,

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:14.292
my vote was to kill
the two of you.

00:00:14.375 --> 00:00:15.708
While we've had to
say goodbye to

00:00:15.792 --> 00:00:17.542
some of the lake's
longest serving residents

00:00:17.625 --> 00:00:18.958
in season four part one,

00:00:19.042 --> 00:00:21.000
it also moved pieces
into place

00:00:21.083 --> 00:00:23.792
for an even more explosive
season finale.

00:00:26.458 --> 00:00:28.083
With a short wait
before it lands,

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:30.500
fans are mulling over
what they think might happen

00:00:30.583 --> 00:00:32.958
when it returns to wrap up
the series for good.

00:00:33.042 --> 00:00:33.917
Here's a hint:

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.417
it involves
a fair amount of death.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.833
Here are four fan theories
about &lt;i&gt;Ozark&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:38.917 --> 00:00:40.708
that will blow your mind.

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:44.333
Be careful if you aren't
up to date:

00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:45.917
spoilers incoming.

00:00:53.083 --> 00:00:53.958
Of course,

00:00:54.042 --> 00:00:55.958
we can't forget one of
the biggest question marks

00:00:56.042 --> 00:00:57.458
that hangs over season four:

00:00:57.542 --> 00:00:59.542
will the Byrdes survive
the car crash?

00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:02.208
The first episode starts
in exhilarating fashion

00:01:02.292 --> 00:01:04.500
as the Byrde family drive
out of the Ozarks

00:01:04.583 --> 00:01:08.125
discussing how there's
only 48 hours left and then…

00:01:08.917 --> 00:01:09.792
Dad!

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:21.333
This scene isn't referenced
again

00:01:21.417 --> 00:01:23.208
throughout the entirety
of season four,

00:01:23.292 --> 00:01:24.542
leading some fans to
speculate that

00:01:24.625 --> 00:01:26.125
it's a flash forward

00:01:26.208 --> 00:01:29.000
taking place after what
we see during this season

00:01:29.083 --> 00:01:32.125
and, possibly,
the very end of the series.

00:01:32.208 --> 00:01:33.625
So, we can move back
to Chicago?

00:01:33.708 --> 00:01:35.292
Yeah. Yes, we can.

00:01:35.375 --> 00:01:38.083
One theory is that it takes
place at the end of the show

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:40.250
foreshadowing
of Byrde's demise.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:41.583
After years of surviving

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:43.750
the violent attentions
of the cartel,

00:01:43.833 --> 00:01:46.458
Kansas city mob, the Snells
and the Langmores,

00:01:46.542 --> 00:01:49.750
the family are taken out by
a simple accident:

00:01:49.833 --> 00:01:51.375
a moment of dark irony

00:01:51.458 --> 00:01:53.875
that would fit with
this show's bleak themes.

00:01:53.958 --> 00:01:55.292
According to another theory,

00:01:55.375 --> 00:01:56.958
it could be that
the Byrdes' end game is

00:01:57.042 --> 00:01:58.375
to go into
witness protection,

00:01:58.458 --> 00:02:00.500
staging an accident
so nobody knows

00:02:00.583 --> 00:02:02.417
they've moved out
of the Ozarks.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:04.083
We know they've worked for
the FBI

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:05.042
throughout season four

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:07.542
and this could be part of
their plan to get out.

00:02:07.625 --> 00:02:09.958
That's why the truck is on
the wrong side of the road

00:02:10.042 --> 00:02:12.375
and doesn't attempt
to swerve out of the way

00:02:12.458 --> 00:02:15.042
because it's all
part of the plan.

00:02:15.125 --> 00:02:17.667
But maybe,
as some fans have suggested,

00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:20.125
the car crash doesn't
actually happen

00:02:20.208 --> 00:02:22.500
and is, instead, symbolic of
the upcoming trouble

00:02:22.583 --> 00:02:25.042
the family are about to have
with both Ruth Langmore

00:02:25.125 --> 00:02:26.458
and Javi Elizonndro.

00:02:26.542 --> 00:02:28.333
Considering we're yet to see

00:02:28.417 --> 00:02:30.042
what comes of
their confrontation,

00:02:30.125 --> 00:02:33.333
it could be a metaphor for
how Ruth and Javi's fight

00:02:33.417 --> 00:02:35.000
will derail
the Byrdes' plans

00:02:35.083 --> 00:02:36.875
to leave the Ozarks
for good.

00:02:36.958 --> 00:02:38.542
We're moving back to Chicago
to keep up.

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:39.625
However,

00:02:39.708 --> 00:02:41.292
it's also been argued that

00:02:41.375 --> 00:02:42.708
the reason the truck
doesn't swerve

00:02:42.792 --> 00:02:45.750
is because it's looking to
actually kill the Byrdes,

00:02:45.833 --> 00:02:48.375
which brings us onto
our next theory.

00:02:48.458 --> 00:02:50.417
We want you to know that
we know that.

00:02:51.458 --> 00:02:52.833
A lot of fans
have speculated that

00:02:52.917 --> 00:02:55.250
one of the Byrdes is going
to be kicking the bucket

00:02:55.333 --> 00:02:57.292
in the second half
of season four

00:02:57.375 --> 00:02:59.708
and there's no end of
theories as to who

00:02:59.792 --> 00:03:01.708
or how many it will be.

00:03:01.792 --> 00:03:03.500
One of the most popular
theories is that

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:06.958
Wendy is unlikely to make it
back to Chicago as the price

00:03:07.042 --> 00:03:09.125
of her ever-growing
rap sheet of felonies grows

00:03:09.208 --> 00:03:11.625
and toll of playing her part
in her brother's murder

00:03:11.708 --> 00:03:13.125
continues to haunt her.

00:03:13.208 --> 00:03:14.750
I can't do this.

00:03:14.833 --> 00:03:15.875
Another suggests that,

00:03:15.958 --> 00:03:18.208
if Ruth dies, then
poor old Three is driving

00:03:18.292 --> 00:03:19.833
the truck
seen in the premiere

00:03:19.917 --> 00:03:21.042
attempting to
get payback for

00:03:21.125 --> 00:03:23.250
the family's involvement
in the death of his cousin,

00:03:23.833 --> 00:03:25.875
as well as the many other
family members

00:03:25.958 --> 00:03:27.250
he's lost over the years.

00:03:29.417 --> 00:03:32.125
One Reddit post even goes
as far to suggest that

00:03:32.208 --> 00:03:33.833
fratricide could be
on the cards,

00:03:33.917 --> 00:03:35.542
theorising that
Charlotte could end up

00:03:35.625 --> 00:03:38.208
killing her brother Jonah
to mirror the sacrifice

00:03:38.292 --> 00:03:39.875
Wendy made with
her brother Ben

00:03:39.958 --> 00:03:43.167
when he became detrimental
to the family business.

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:46.167
Maybe their trip to a crypt
at the end of season four

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:48.333
is teasing
their potential fate.

00:03:48.417 --> 00:03:50.625
Maybe if you kill me you can
make one of these, too.

00:03:51.167 --> 00:03:52.875
With these theories
floating about,

00:03:52.958 --> 00:03:54.875
it's clear that fans think
the Byrdes

00:03:54.958 --> 00:03:56.333
will have their wings
clipped.

00:03:56.417 --> 00:03:57.875
We like your odds!

00:03:58.792 --> 00:03:59.708
In season four,

00:03:59.792 --> 00:04:02.042
we're introduced to private
investigator Mel Sattem

00:04:02.125 --> 00:04:04.542
who's looking for
information on Helen Pierce,

00:04:04.625 --> 00:04:07.750
the cartel handler who met
a particularly gruesome end

00:04:07.833 --> 00:04:08.958
in season three,

00:04:09.042 --> 00:04:11.792
asking the people of the
Ozarks if they've seen her.

00:04:11.875 --> 00:04:13.125
Anything at all
from Helen Pierce?

00:04:13.208 --> 00:04:14.750
No, sorry.

00:04:14.833 --> 00:04:15.708
However,

00:04:15.792 --> 00:04:17.875
while Mel says he was hired
by Pierce's husband

00:04:17.958 --> 00:04:19.500
to get a signature
on their divorce,

00:04:19.583 --> 00:04:21.542
some fans aren't convinced.

00:04:21.625 --> 00:04:24.083
This theory goes that Sattem
is actually working for

00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:27.625
Omar Navarro as his eyes
and ears on the ground,

00:04:27.708 --> 00:04:30.708
which is why Omar knew
where Marty and Wendy hid

00:04:30.792 --> 00:04:32.167
Charlotte and Jonah.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.083
Another person he could
end up working with is

00:04:34.167 --> 00:04:36.167
FBI agent Maya Miller.

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:37.958
We see the pair chatting
over the phone

00:04:38.042 --> 00:04:40.292
in the season four part one
finale.

00:04:40.375 --> 00:04:42.583
And, with Maya arresting
Omar Navarro

00:04:42.667 --> 00:04:43.875
against her boss' orders,

00:04:43.958 --> 00:04:46.542
she could soon be
in need of some friends.

00:04:46.625 --> 00:04:49.167
If Mel isn't working for
Omar Navarro,

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:52.792
could he decide to help her
unravel the cartel's plans?

00:04:52.875 --> 00:04:53.958
Big fan.

00:04:54.583 --> 00:04:56.292
Now, we know
what you're thinking.

00:04:56.375 --> 00:04:59.583
Of course Wendy's troubled
brother, Ben, is dead.

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:02.958
After all, we saw Marty burn
his body at the crematorium.

00:05:03.042 --> 00:05:04.333
Well, this is where

00:05:04.417 --> 00:05:07.083
the slightly more out there
fan theory comes in,

00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:09.500
as some believe
that wasn't Ben's body

00:05:09.583 --> 00:05:11.125
as we never saw his face.

00:05:11.208 --> 00:05:12.042
On top of that,

00:05:12.125 --> 00:05:14.750
we never see Nelson,
the cartel hitman,

00:05:14.833 --> 00:05:17.083
actually murder Ben,
so there's a chance that

00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:19.500
the cartel might be
holding on to him

00:05:19.583 --> 00:05:20.792
for leverage.

00:05:20.875 --> 00:05:22.917
Although considering
season four deals with

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.083
the fall out from his murder

00:05:24.167 --> 00:05:26.333
from missing posters
plastered all over town

00:05:26.417 --> 00:05:28.375
to Jonah becoming
more antagonistic

00:05:28.458 --> 00:05:30.917
towards his parents for
their role in Ben's death…

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:32.958
I was upset because mum
killed Ben.

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:34.667
…It's safe to say that

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:36.708
we shouldn't expect to see
Ben again.

00:05:36.792 --> 00:05:38.250
But you never know.

00:05:38.333 --> 00:05:39.458
What did you expect, Wendy?

00:05:40.958 --> 00:05:42.958
And those are some of
the biggest fan theories

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:44.667
circulating at the moment.

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:46.667
Of course, the only way
to know for sure is

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:48.625
to head back to &lt;i&gt;Ozark&lt;/i&gt;
season four.

00:05:48.708 --> 00:05:50.708
Part two airs in April.

00:05:50.792 --> 00:05:52.125
While you wait,
we'd love to know

00:05:52.208 --> 00:05:53.750
what you think will happen
to the Byrdes

00:05:53.833 --> 00:05:55.083
in the comments below.

00:05:55.167 --> 00:05:56.375
And don't forget to
hit the subscribe

00:05:56.458 --> 00:05:59.375
and notifications button
on Still Watching Netflix

00:05:59.458 --> 00:06:00.458
to discover more about

00:06:00.542 --> 00:06:03.000
your favourite TV shows
and films.

